    "# SPD3000 guided hardware test\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy this file to `test_spd3000.ipynb`, select the Python environment containing this checkout, and run the cells in order.\n",
    "The notebook imports the installed `siglent_spd3000` package, so its results exercise the actual driver implementation rather than a duplicate test script.\n",
    "Read-only cells come first, followed by direct hardware-control tests.\n",
    "The complete acceptance procedure remains in [`.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md`](.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Run this notebook only with the power supply isolated from sensitive hardware and connected only to a correctly rated dummy load or measurement instrument, so unexpected voltage, current, or output settings cannot damage anything.**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Keep the front panel accessible, and stop immediately if an output cannot be disabled.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "notebook-imports"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Imports used throughout this notebook\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import atexit\n",
    "from pprint import pprint\n",
    "from time import monotonic, sleep\n",
    "\n",
    "import siglent_spd3000 as spd"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Connection settings\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit the `connect()` arguments in the first code cell for the connection being tested.\n",
    "Optional VISA resource-discovery and gateway-specific connection examples follow it.\n",
    "Replace `<TYPE>` with a `spd.ConnectionType` member such as `SOCKET`, `VXI11`, `VISA`, or `GATEWAY`, and replace `<IDENTIFIER>` with its matching address or resource.\n",
    "Use a power-supply hostname or IP address for `SOCKET` and `VXI11`, a complete enumerated VISA resource for `VISA`, or `localhost`/`host[:port]` for `GATEWAY`.\n",
    "The two commented connection-specific arguments explain when to enable them; leave both commented for raw socket, VXI-11, system-default VISA, or an unauthenticated local gateway."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "connection-settings"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if \"psu\" in globals():\n",
    "    psu.close()\n",
    "\n",
    "psu = spd.SPD3000.connect(\n",
    "    connection=spd.ConnectionType.<TYPE>,  # e.g., SOCKET, VXI11, VISA, GATEWAY\n",
    "    identifier=\"<IDENTIFIER>\",  # e.g., instrument IP, VISA resource, or gateway host[:port]\n",
    "    timeout_s=5.0,  # communication timeout in seconds\n",
    "    min_command_interval_ms=100.0,  # delay between instrument commands in milliseconds\n",
    "    verify_writes_globally=False,  # True adds readback after supported writes\n",
    "    # visa_backend=\"@py\",  # Uncomment only to force PyVISA-py for a VISA connection.\n",
    "    # token=spd.load_gateway_auth(\"gateway-auth.toml\"),  # Uncomment for an authenticated gateway.\n",
    ")\n",
    "atexit.register(psu.close)\n",
    "print(psu)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
