  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Write verification\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell reapplies the current CH1 voltage, current, and output settings without changing their logical values.\n",
    "Inside `psu.verify_writes()`, each write is followed by its documented readback and raises `SPD3000VerificationError` if the returned value does not match."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "current_voltage = psu.ch1.voltage\n",
    "current_limit = psu.ch1.current\n",
    "current_output = psu.ch1.output\n",
    "\n",
    "with psu.verify_writes():\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = current_voltage\n",
    "    psu.ch1.current = current_limit\n",
    "    psu.ch1.output = current_output\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"CH1 voltage, current, and output writes were verified.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Batch execution\n",
    "\n",
    "Batch execution postpones I/O until the context or decorated function exits and sends the collected commands as one non-interleaved sequence.\n",
    "`responses` is an ordinary list that stays empty inside the block and is extended on successful exit with only explicit user-query results in source order; writes and automatic verification readbacks are omitted.\n",
    "Batching guarantees ordering and non-interleaving, not rollback."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.1 Context manager and responses\n",
    "\n",
    "Setters add writes, while property reads and query methods add parsed results to `responses` when the context exits.\n",
    "Because `responses` is a normal list, it supports indexing, iteration, slicing, and unpacking."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with psu.batch() as responses:\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "    psu.ch1.current = 0.1\n",
    "    psu.ch1.output = False\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.voltage\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.current\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.output\n",
    "\n",
    "print(type(responses))\n",
    "print(responses)\n",
    "ch1_voltage, ch1_current_limit, ch1_output = responses\n",
    "print(ch1_voltage, ch1_current_limit, ch1_output)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.2 Decorator\n",
    "\n",
    "`@psu.batch` uses the same batch context and resolves deferred values contained in the function's returned built-in containers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@psu.batch\n",
    "def configure_and_read():\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "    return psu.ch1.voltage, psu.measure.voltage(spd.Channel.CH1)\n",
    "\n",
    "ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage = configure_and_read()\n",
    "print(ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.3 Batch with write verification\n",
    "\n",
    "Combining `psu.batch()` with `psu.verify_writes()` keeps writes and their readbacks in one batch.\n",
    "In the first cell, the automatic readbacks perform verification but do not appear in `responses`; only the two explicit property queries are returned."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with psu.batch() as responses, psu.verify_writes():\n",
    "    psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "    psu.ch1.current = 0.1\n",
    "    psu.ch1.output = False\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.voltage\n",
    "    _ = psu.ch1.current\n",
    "\n",
    "verified_voltage, verified_current_limit = responses\n",
    "print(verified_voltage, verified_current_limit)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The second cell demonstrates the same combination in decorator form.\n",
    "`@psu.batch` supplies the enclosing batch, while the nested `psu.verify_writes()` adds automatic readback only for the voltage write inside that context.\n",
    "After the complete batch executes, the decorator resolves the returned voltage-setpoint and live-measurement queries into ordinary `float` values before returning them to the caller.\n",
    "If CH1 output remains disabled, a 1.0 V setpoint together with a live measurement near 0 V is expected."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@psu.batch\n",
    "def configure_and_read():\n",
    "    with psu.verify_writes():\n",
    "        psu.ch1.voltage = 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    return psu.ch1.voltage, psu.measure.voltage(spd.Channel.CH1)\n",
    "\n",
    "ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage = configure_and_read()\n",
    "print(ch1_set_voltage, ch1_measured_voltage)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.4 Gateway multi-client batch isolation\n",
    "\n",
    "Run this write test only through the gateway and with CH1 isolated from sensitive hardware.\n",
    "Four independent clients wait on one barrier, sleep for different random durations shorter than `psu.settings.min_command_interval`, and then submit batches containing `set voltage → set current → query voltage → query current`.\n",
    "While each request is queued or executing, gateway heartbeats keep its client connection alive without exposing intermediate values or changing batch isolation.\n",
    "The randomized arrivals scramble client order while keeping all submissions close together; every returned V/I pair must match the values set earlier in that same batch, which would not be reliable if commands from other clients were interleaved.\n",
    "The cell disables CH1 output before testing and restores its original voltage, current, and output state afterward."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "gateway-batch-isolation"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor, as_completed\n",
    "from random import Random\n",
    "from threading import Barrier\n",
    "from time import sleep\n",
    "\n",
    "assert psu.connection_type is spd.ConnectionType.GATEWAY\n",
    "assert psu.connection_identifier is not None\n",
    "assert psu.settings.min_command_interval > 0\n",
    "\n",
    "original_voltage = psu.ch1.voltage\n",
    "original_current = psu.ch1.current\n",
    "original_output = psu.ch1.output\n",
    "gateway_token = spd.load_gateway_auth(\"gateway-auth.toml\")\n",
    "client_cases = (\n",
    "    (1, 0.5, 0.05),\n",
    "    (2, 0.6, 0.06),\n",
    "    (3, 0.7, 0.07),\n",
    "    (4, 0.8, 0.08),\n",
    ")\n",
    "start_barrier = Barrier(len(client_cases))\n",
    "randomizer = Random()\n",
    "scheduled_cases = [\n",
    "    (*case, randomizer.uniform(0.0, psu.settings.min_command_interval * 0.9))\n",
    "    for case in client_cases\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def set_and_read_in_one_batch(\n",
    "    client_number: int, voltage_v: float, current_a: float, delay_s: float\n",
    ") -> tuple[int, float, float, float, float, float]:\n",
    "    with spd.SPD3000.connect(\n",
    "        connection=spd.ConnectionType.GATEWAY,\n",
    "        identifier=psu.connection_identifier,\n",
    "        timeout_s=psu.settings.timeout,\n",
    "        min_command_interval_ms=psu.settings.min_command_interval * 1000.0,\n",
    "        token=gateway_token,\n",
    "    ) as client:\n",
    "        start_barrier.wait(timeout=10.0)\n",
    "        sleep(delay_s)\n",
    "        with client.batch() as responses:\n",
    "            client.ch1.voltage = voltage_v\n",
    "            client.ch1.current = current_a\n",
    "            _ = client.ch1.voltage\n",
    "            _ = client.ch1.current\n",
    "    read_voltage_v, read_current_a = responses\n",
    "    return client_number, delay_s, voltage_v, current_a, read_voltage_v, read_current_a\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    psu.ch1.output = False\n",
    "    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=len(scheduled_cases)) as pool:\n",
    "        futures = [pool.submit(set_and_read_in_one_batch, *case) for case in scheduled_cases]\n",
    "        for future in as_completed(futures):\n",
    "            client_number, delay_s, voltage_v, current_a, read_voltage_v, read_current_a = (\n",
    "                future.result()\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            assert read_voltage_v == voltage_v\n",
    "            assert read_current_a == current_a\n",
    "            print(\n",
    "                f\"Client {client_number}: delay={delay_s * 1000:.1f} ms, \"\n",
    "                f\"set/read={voltage_v}/{read_voltage_v} V, \"\n",
    "                f\"{current_a}/{read_current_a} A\"\n",
    "            )\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    with psu.batch():\n",
    "        psu.ch1.voltage = original_voltage\n",
    "        psu.ch1.current = original_current\n",
    "        psu.ch1.output = original_output"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Repeated-query stability\n",
    "\n",
    "Repeated identity and status reads help reveal stale, truncated, or mistimed responses without changing hardware settings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "READ_ITERATIONS = 10\n",
    "started = monotonic()\n",
    "for iteration in range(1, READ_ITERATIONS + 1):\n",
    "    assert psu.idn.model is psu.model\n",
    "    current_status = psu.system.status\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"{iteration:03d}: status=0x{current_status.raw:04X}, \"\n",
    "        f\"mode={current_status.operating_mode.value}\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "print(f\"Completed {READ_ITERATIONS} iterations in {monotonic() - started:.2f} s\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Model-specific read-only checks\n",
    "\n",
    "Network settings and front-panel lock state are queried only when the detected model documents those queries.\n",
    "Some SPD3303X firmware/connection combinations do not answer the separately documented `*LOCK?` command; that optional check is reported without stopping the remaining tests."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if psu.capabilities.network:\n",
    "    print(psu.network.settings)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Network queries are not supported by {psu.model.value}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "LOCK_QUERY_RESPONDS = False\n",
    "if psu.capabilities.lock_query:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        print(f\"Front panel locked: {psu.locked}\")\n",
    "    except (spd.SPD3000TimeoutError, spd.SPD3000ProtocolError) as exc:\n",
    "        print(\n",
    "            f\"Warning: *LOCK? is documented for {psu.model.value} but did not return a usable \"\n",
    "            f\"response on this connection ({exc}). Later lock-state assertions will be skipped; \"\n",
    "            \"verify lock and unlock at the front panel.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        LOCK_QUERY_RESPONDS = True\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Lock-state query is not supported by {psu.model.value}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Read-only semantic and raw batches\n",
    "\n",
    "The semantic batch returns ordinary parsed Python objects, while the raw batch returns SCPI strings aligned with its commands.\n",
    "Both paths submit their two queries as one non-interleaved batch, which is especially important when the gateway is serving multiple clients."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with psu.batch() as semantic_responses:\n",
    "    _ = psu.idn\n",
    "    _ = psu.system.status\n",
    "\n",
    "batch_identity, batch_status = semantic_responses\n",
    "print(batch_identity)\n",
    "print(batch_status)\n",
    "assert batch_identity.model is psu.model\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_batch = psu.scpi.execute([spd.Query(\"*IDN?\"), spd.Query(\"SYST:STAT?\")])\n",
    "print(raw_batch.values)\n",
    "assert len(raw_batch.values) == 2\n",
    "assert all(isinstance(value, str) for value in raw_batch.values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Optional error-queue read\n",
    "\n",
    "Reading `psu.system.error` removes one entry from the instrument error queue, so this diagnostic is opt-in even though it sends no write command."
   ]
